# Log Normalization

Security logs originate from many systems, each with its own format.

Normalization converts raw events into a structured format.

For example:

Raw SSH log:

```
Failed password for invalid user admin from 203.0.113.77 port 22 ssh2
```

After parsing:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Username | admin |
| Source IP | 203.0.113.77 |
| Event Type | Failed Login |
| Protocol | SSH |
| Port | 22 |

Normalization improves search, correlation, and detection accuracy.

